#!/bin/sh
# Load zrn-therm at boot (zrn-therm.service), before zrn-charge: the battery
# temperature, measured (power/thermistors/README.md). Without it zrn-charge
# sees the temperature as unknown and allows 5 V only.
#
# Unattended phone: a mark is on the disk while it loads. Found at the next
# boot, the load never finished (the phone froze or reset): it is not loaded
# again until someone looks and clears the failed mark. The shell shows a
# notification while the mark is there (ztnotifyd), and Settings > Battery
# has "Try again", which runs, as root through sudo (one rule, this command
# with --retry only):
#
#   zrn-therm-load --retry	clear the failed mark and load it now
#
# By hand, the same: sudo rm /var/lib/zrn-therm/load-failed; sudo zrn-therm-load
D=/var/lib/zrn-therm
M=$D/loading
F=$D/load-failed
# the running kernel's own build (another release's is refused: vermagic)
KO=/usr/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/extra/zrn-therm.ko
case "${1:-}" in
--retry)
	[ -e "$F" ] && { echo "zrn-therm: load-failed cleared by hand ($(cat "$F" 2>/dev/null))"; rm -f "$F"; sync; } ;;
'') ;;
*) echo "usage: zrn-therm-load [--retry]" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
[ -d /sys/module/zrn_therm ] && exit 0
mkdir -p "$D"
if [ -e "$M" ]; then
	mv -f "$M" "$F"
	sync
fi
if [ -e "$F" ]; then
	echo "zrn-therm: a load never finished ($F): not loading it; the battery temperature stays unknown (5 V only)"
	exit 0
fi
if [ ! -f "$KO" ]; then
	echo "zrn-therm: no module for $(uname -r) ($KO); the battery temperature stays unknown (5 V only)"
	exit 0
fi
date +%s > "$M"
sync
if insmod "$KO"; then
	echo "zrn-therm: loaded"
else
	echo "zrn-therm: insmod failed; the battery temperature stays unknown (5 V only)"
fi
rm -f "$M"
sync
exit 0
